    "updated_at": "2022-01-27T10:54:15Z",
    "body": "> I don't use canvas so i convert base64 by using png encoder and Buffer.from () api. But this operations consume performance a lot especially as big size image.\r\n\r\nThis makes it sound unlikely that base64 encoding/decoding is where your bottleneck is. Have you measured / confirmed that?\r\n\r\nYou mentioned `Buffer.from` and a “png encoder.” The first is a Node API and the latter I’m guessing refers to a specific JS library. Even if you don’t use canvas for rendering the image, the broader canvas API exposes the browser’s natively-implemented PNG-encoding capability. If the library is reimplementing this functionality in the JS layer, it will never be as fast as what the browser already provides.",
